Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Engine-side audio bracket set for the wave-35 Phase 12 instrumentation
contract (`docs/PHASE11-WAVE-35-CONTRACT.md` § 8). Pre-instrumentation
iter for the wave-36+ Phase 12 audio-cost-attribution program; the
~31 ms unattributed audio cost from `audio_cost_attribution_unknown.md`
gets decomposed into engine-side (this patch) + audio-thread + IRQ-5
sub-buckets (sibling SDL/0054 covers SDL-side).

Context. Wave-33 § 7 ranking put "Phase 12 Pixtone-decouple" at rank #1
based on the premise that Pixtone synthesizes per-frame inside audio
IRQ. Tree-grep revealed the premise is wrong: Pixtone is ALREADY pre-
rendered at init (`stPXSound::render()` at Pixtone.cpp:157 runs once
per .pxt slot in `Pixtone::init()` at line 318; MIX_Audio cached;
audio thread does memcpy not synthesis). The original Phase 12
"decouple" framing therefore had no work to do. Team-lead Option (b)
pivot per `reconcile_deepdive_against_tree_facts.md`: instrumentation-
first; measure the real bottleneck; then attack the dominant slice in
wave-36+.

Mechanism. 3 RAII timer brackets in NXE::Diag namespace
(diagnostic_timers.h) + 6 per-block counter pairs (accum_ns + count) in
Renderer.cpp's NXE::Diag storage block + audit-flush emit one-liner
gated on FLIP_INSTR. Bracket call sites:

- MidiScheduler::tick body (per-frame from SoundManager::runFade for
  opl3/wb/midi_stub backends). Captures MIDI event dispatch + per-
  backend register writes (OPL3 ADL writes; WB MPU-401 writes;
  midi_stub LOG_DEBUG silence).

- Pixtone::play body (per-SFX-trigger). Captures MIX_StopTrack +
  MIX_SetTrackAudio + MIX_PlayTrack chain cost.

- Pixtone::playResampled body (per-SFX-trigger; SHARED accumulator
  with Pixtone::play since both are per-SFX-trigger dispatch). On
  first call per (slot, percent), includes SDL_AudioStream resample
  cost; subsequent calls hit the cache.

- Pixtone::stop body (per-SFX-event). Captures MIX_StopTrack call cost
  + bookkeeping.

NOT bracketed (already covered elsewhere):

- organyaStreamCallback body — patch 0062 AudioMixerTimer covers it
  via g_audio_mix_accum_ns_block (audio thread; same TU reads).
- IRQ-5 ISR work — patch 0100 doskutsu_audio_irq_count +
  doskutsu_audio_irq_wall_us already export this; flush-instr's
  decomp reads them directly.
- SDL_mixer MIX_Mixer mix-down — sdl-engine's SDL/0054 lane.
- SDL3-DOS audio thread main loop — sdl-engine's SDL/0054 lane.

Gating. SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_P12_AUDIO_INSTR=1 (strict-"1"; default OFF).
Cost when off: ~zero (cached static-const-bool; -O3 hoists destructor
guard). Cost when on: 2 SDL_GetTicksNS reads per bracketed function
+ 1 accumulator add + 1 counter increment on the on-path.

Per-call frequency in steady-state gameplay (Tier-2 OPL3 First Cave
heavy-music as the wave-35 target):
- midi_tick: ~100 calls per 100-flip block (one per frame)
- pixtone_play: ~5-20 calls per block (sparse SFX triggers; rate
  depends on combat density)
- pixtone_stop: ~5-20 calls per block (mirrors play)

Total instrumentation overhead at peak: ~ 130 × 2 × ~30 cycles
per RDTSC read on PODP83 ≈ ~25 µs / block (0.0003% measurement
distortion at 31 ms baseline). Negligible.

Audit-flush emit (gated on FLIP_INSTR, same as flip-stat / flip-body-
stat / bg-subregion families):

  [p12-audio n=100 midi_tick_us=N midi_tick_count=N
   pixtone_play_us=N pixtone_play_count=N
   pixtone_stop_us=N pixtone_stop_count=N]

ns→us conversion in emit (accumulator stored in ns for precision; emit
in µs for readability). Counter equation
  midi_tick_count ≈ 100  (per-frame)
  pixtone_play_count + pixtone_stop_count ≈ SFX-event-rate × 100/fps
  midi_tick_us / midi_tick_count = avg-µs-per-tick
holds when env-var is on across the full block.

All 6 counters reset unconditionally on audit-flush exit. Sample
contents are overwritten by next block's brackets; idx-style reset
zeros them for the next emit cycle.

Cross-thread NOTE. Engine-side brackets are MAIN THREAD only. No
volatile / atomic semantics needed; the cooperative DOS scheduler
doesn't preempt main-thread code while it's in these bodies. Sibling
SDL/0054 handles audio-thread brackets and uses the patch 0062 / 0100
volatile-uint pattern for cross-thread reads at audit-flush.

Coordination with SDL/0054 (sdl-engine's lane). Same env-var
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_P12_AUDIO_INSTR=1 gates both bracket sets so single
SET in the BAT enables both engine-side + SDL-side measurement. SDL/-
0054 emit line will be `[p12-sdl ...]` (different prefix; same FLIP_-
INSTR gate; sdl-engine designs the field set).

Wave-35 ride-along fps lever (per `realhw_iter_must_test_fps_idea.md`
that instrumentation iters MUST ride along with a fps probe). Initial
contract proposed patch 0132 cross-scrolltype extension of wave-34's
slot 0130 to BK_FOLLOWFG; tree-grep revealed slot 0130 already covers
all cacheable scrolltypes (BK_FIXED / BK_FOLLOWFG / BK_PARALLAX /
BK_FASTLEFT) by virtue of being in the post-switch generic branch.
flush-instr coordination in flight on the actual wave-35 ride-along —
likely slot 0117 extension to mds_tilemap_bg drawTileFast (rank #2 in
session-snapshot 2026-05-08 § 6; -1 to -2 ms predicted; mechanism
already proven in wave-33).

Files. New: src/Utils/diagnostic_timers.h 6 counter externs + 3 RAII
timer structs + forward-decl; src/graphics/Renderer.cpp 6 counter
storage + _abl_p12_audio_instr() env-helper + forward-decl + file-
scope wrapper + audit-flush emit/reset block; src/sound/MidiScheduler-
.cpp diagnostic_timers.h include + P12MidiTickTimer RAII at tick()
entry; src/sound/Pixtone.cpp diagnostic_timers.h include +
P12PixtonePlayTimer RAII at play()/playResampled() entries +
P12PixtoneStopTimer RAII at stop() entry. docs/BOOT.md entry. ~200
LOC including comments.

Smoke. Builds clean at i486 -O3 -funroll-loops -fno-rtti. New strings
in binary: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_P12_AUDIO_INSTR env-var symbol,
[p12-audio n=100 ...] emit template. All prior slot markers (slot
0128 TILE_BOUNDS_SKIP, slot 0129 snd-shutdown[3.5/6], slot 0130
BG_SUBREGION_BLIT, slot 0126 thrashing-detect engaged) retained.
Slot 0127 Lever B markers still absent (wave-32 revert intact).
Real-HW gate: wave-35 production PLAY1 (env unset; instrumentation
silent; pure fps measurement of ride-along fps lever) vs PLAY2
(SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_P12_AUDIO_INSTR=1 + FLIP_INSTR=1; counters emit).

Predicted measurement outcome (per flush-instr's contract § 5.4 +
audio_cost_attribution_unknown.md):
- midi_tick_us per block: 0.1-2 ms (one MIDI event dispatch per frame
  + per-backend write — OPL3 has ~5-30 register writes per tempo-tick
  event); flush-instr's decomp validates whether the OPL3 backend is
  the dominant slice of "main-thread audio work" or not.
- pixtone_play_us / pixtone_stop_us: small (~tens of µs per call;
  ~hundreds of µs per block in combat-heavy scenes).
- The bulk of the ~31 ms unattributed cost likely lives in SDL/0054's
  audio-thread brackets, not here. This patch's main contribution is
  ruling out engine-side main-thread audio work as the dominant
  attribution.

Architectural classification. Pure instrumentation; no behavior
change. 0 fps direct impact (counters update + per-frame guard;
~25 µs/block overhead negligible). Wave-35 ride-along fps gain comes
from the separate ride-along lever (TBD with flush-instr).

STOP-and-ack hygiene. The "slot 0132 redundant with slot 0130 for
BK_FOLLOWFG" question was caught via cross-domain grep BEFORE
authoring 0132; flagged to flush-instr for scope re-pick. Slot 0131
is uncontroversial; no design ambiguity.
